    "description": {
      "source": "https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/CBC_J.htm",
      "status": "documented",
      "value": "The complete blood count (CBC) with 5-part differential counts red blood cells (RBCs), white blood cells (WBCs), and platelets; measures hemoglobin; estimates the red cells’ volume and sorts the WBCs into subtypes. A CBC is a routine blood test used to evaluate your overall health and detect a wide range of disorders, including anemia, infection, and leukemia."
